{
  "id": "sawtooth-waves",
  "term": "sawtooth waves",
  "definition": "Sawtooth waves are a non-sinusoidal alternating-current waveform with a ramped shape that can be delivered in transcranial alternating current stimulation (tACS). In this context, they can be set with either a positive or negative ramp direction, and their EEG recording artifact is described as easier to remove than that produced by a sine wave.",
